en or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Would Rather for What Is Preferable", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the expression <span class=\"strong italic\">would rather</span> to ask for or express preference. We generally used its contracted form (<span class=\"strong italic\">'d rather</span>), followed by the basic or infinitive form of the verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Examples: <br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I would rather celebrate music and life in unison with an entire city!</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">You'd rather enjoy the summer while it lasts!</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather warn you though: you might want to come back every year after that!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the expression in its negative form, too. For this, you use the expression <span class=\"strong italic\">not</span> right after <span class=\"italic\">would rather</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">We'd rather not be in crowded places.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">You'd rather not miss the festival.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather not spend the whole day at the festival.</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Questions With How + adjective", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">How + adjective</span> in a question if you want to know how someone or something is.", "type": "describer"}